===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} A greatly [[exaggerated]], [[fantastic]] [[story]].
#: {{ux|en|He returned on Monday with a '''tall tale''' about a 100-pound fish he had caught.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|work={{w|National Geographic Magazine}}|date=August 4, 2020|author=Richard Conniff|url=https://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2020/09/they-may-look-goofy-but-ostriches-are-nobodys-fool-feature/|title=They may look goofy, but ostriches are nobody’s fool
|passage=The head-in-sand idea is a threadbare, 2,000-year-old hand-me-down from the Roman naturalist Pliny, who sometimes passed on '''tall tales'''.}}

